5. Potential points of failure
Potential failures include:
The task ID may not identify an existing task.
mark_as_done() may not be called.
The task object may fail to update.
The storage/persistence operation may fail.
The application may crash before the updated task is saved.
An invalid task or missing data could cause an error.
6. How the application persists the changes
The task completion process begins when the task manager receives a request to mark a task as complete. The task's mark_as_done() method changes its status to TaskStatus.DONE, records the completion time in completed_at, and updates updated_at. The updated task then needs to be passed to the application's storage layer so that the changes persist. Potential failures include an invalid task ID, failure to update the task, or failure to save the updated task
